  "id": "static-response",
  "term": "static response",
  "definition": "Static response is the steady, ongoing firing pattern a cold-sensitive nerve ending shows at a constant temperature. It refers to regular temperature-dependent activity, ranging from tonic firing to regular bursting, as distinct from the brief change in firing that occurs during rapid temperature shifts.",
